From: Caboose <caboose@invalid>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 41/41] Name the shader modules the phone keeps by their hash

With hello feature 0x2000 the phone keeps every SPIR-V module a computer
sends, under its BLAKE3 hash, across sessions (docs/gpu-live.md, "Shader
cache"). vkCreateShaderModule asks once per process for the keys the phone
holds (SHADER_INVENTORY, after every reply the encoder still owes), and
then sends a 48-byte token instead of the code of a module it holds or that
the process already sent on its single device stream. The key covers the
bytes actually sent, after 0037's cull-distance rewrite. Modules under 256
bytes, a failed inventory and a process with several device streams send
code as before (caboose-shader-cache/shader_cache.h).
